  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a grid of size N×MN\\times MN×M (N(N(N and MMM are both even))), where each cell of the grid has value 000.\n\nLet RiR_iRi​ denote the bitwise XOR of all elements of the ithi^{th}ith row and CiC_iCi​ denote the bitwise XOR of all elements of the ithi^{th}ith column.\n\nUgliness of a grid is defined as ∑i=1NRi+∑i=1MCi\\displaystyle{\\sum_{i=1}^{N} R_i  + \\sum_{i=1}^{M} C_i}i=1∑N​Ri​+i=1∑M​Ci​.\n\nLet F(K)F(K)F(K) denote the **minimum** ugliness possible after setting the value of **exactly** KKK cells of this grid as 111.\n\nFind the value ∑i=1N⋅MF(i)\\sum_{i=1}^{N \\cdot M} F(i)∑i=1N⋅M​F(i).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two space-separated **even** integers N,MN, MN,M — the number of rows and the number of columns respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the value ∑i=1N⋅MF(i)\\sum_{i=1}^{N \\cdot M} F(i)∑i=1N⋅M​F(i).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N,M≤109;&nbsp;N1 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^9; \\ N1≤N,M≤109;&nbsp;N and MMM are even."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 2\n2 6\n4 2",
        "output": "6\n18\n12",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\n\nFor K=1K = 1K=1: R1=1R_1 = 1R1​=1, R2=0R_2 = 0R2​=0, C1=0C_1 = 0C1​=0, C2=1C_2 = 1C2​=1. So F(1)=2F(1) = 2F(1)=2.\n\n\n\nFor K=2K = 2K=2: R1=0R_1 = 0R1​=0, R2=0R_2 = 0R2​=0, C1=1C_1 = 1C1​=1, C2=1C_2 = 1C2​=1. So F(2)=2F(2) = 2F(2)=2.\n\n\n\nFor K=3K = 3K=3: R1=0R_1 = 0R1​=0, R2=1R_2 = 1R2​=1, C1=1C_1 = 1C1​=1, C2=0C_2 = 0C2​=0. So F(3)=2F(3) = 2F(3)=2.\n\n\n\nFor K=4K = 4K=4: R1=0R_1 = 0R1​=0, R2=0R_2 = 0R2​=0, C1=0C_1 = 0C1​=0, C2=0C_2 = 0C2​=0. So F(4)=0F(4) = 0F(4)=0."
      }
    ]
  },
